llyBoundedVariationOn.stoppedProcess`, and `ProbabilityTheory.locallyBoundedVariationOn_stoppedProcess_indicator`. The local theorem `ProbabilityTheory.IsLocalMartingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation` now compiles with no internal `sorry`, reducing entirely to the true-martingale bridge `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation`.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the discrete predictable uniqueness wrapper `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation_discrete` from Mathlib's `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable'`. The true-martingale wrapper `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation` now handles the bottom-time case directly and delegates only the non-initial analytic bridge to `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation_noninitial`.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the deterministic predictable-past measurability layer: `MeasureTheory.Filtration.measurable_prod_mk_predictable_past` and `MeasureTheory.IsStronglyPredictable.stronglyMeasurable_past`. The public non-initial theorem `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation_noninitial` now derives the exact past-measurability hypothesis from strong predictability and delegates only the analytic jump-removal/continuous finite-variation core to `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation_noninitial_analytic`.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the first conditional-expectation reductions for predictable finite-variation uniqueness: `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation_past_measurable_value` and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation_past_measurable_zero_increment`. The public analytic theorem `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation_noninitial_analytic` now has no internal `sorry` and delegates only