ork is to prove the zero-square-integral premise from partitions, bounded continuous paths, finite variation, and dominated convergence, then feed it into the active reduction.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the bounded deterministic finite-partition infrastructure for the square-integral route: `Finset.sum_range_sub_consecutive`, `MeasureTheory.Martingale.partition_increment_sum_eq_terminal`, `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_partition_cross_increment_eq_zero`, `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integrable_partition_increment_mul_increment_of_bound`, `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integrable_partition_sq_increment_of_bound`, `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integrable_partition_sq_increment_sum_of_bound`, `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_partition_sq_increment_sum_of_bound`, `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_partition_cross_increment_eq_zero_of_bound`, and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integrable_sq_terminal_of_ae_bound`.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integrable_partition_value_mul_increment_of_bound` and the closed integrated finite-square expansion `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_sq_terminal_eq_partition_sq_sum_of_bound`. The predictable finite-variation bridge has advanced past finite partition algebra; the next missing checkpoint is the bounded-continuous/refining-partition dominated-convergence argument proving the zero terminal square integral.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/QuadraticVariationBrownian.lean` now provides the deterministic time process and all Brownian fixed-time quadratic-variation helpers: `ProbabilityTheory.brownianDeterministicTime`, `ProbabilityTheory.isCadlag_brownian_sq_sub_time`, `ProbabilityTheory.stronglyAdapted_brownianDeterministicTime`, `ProbabilityTheory.isStronglyPredictable_brownianDeterministicTime`, `ProbabilityTheory.isStronglyProgressive_brownianDeterministicTime`, `ProbabilityTheory.isCadlag_brownianDeterministicTime`, `ProbabilityTheory.monotone_brownianDeterministicTime`, `ProbabilityTheory.brownianDeterministicTime_bot_eq_zero`, `ProbabilityTheory.hasIntegrableSup_brownianDeterministicTime`, and `ProbabilityTheory.hasLocallyIntegrableSup_brownianDeterministicTime`.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/QuadraticVariationBrownian.lean` now provides the exact fixed-time Brownian quadratic-variation theorem `ProbabilityTheory.quadraticVariation_brownian (t : ℝ≥0) : brownianQuadraticVariation t =ᵐ[gaussianLimit] fun _ => (t : ℝ)`. The target file has no internal `sorry`; the theorem still depends transitively on the open generic square-norm, predictable finite-variation uniqueness, and weak local Doob-Meyer proof debts.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the variation-bounded refining-partition dominated-convergence endpoint `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_sq_terminal_eq_zero_of_refining_partitions`. It combines the finite square expansion with `BoundedVariationOn.sq_increment_sum_le_uniform_bound` and `MeasureTheory.tendsto_integral_of_dominated_convergence`; the active predictable finite-variation bridge now needs the bounded-continuous finite-variation square-integral-zero step, then jump/localization removal.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the deterministic-modulus variation-bound endpoint `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_sq_terminal_eq_zero_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound`. It derives partition bounds from the horizon bound, gets square-increment convergence from `BoundedVariationOn.sq_increment_sum_tendsto_zero_of_uniform_bound`, and calls the closed refining-partition dominated-convergence lemma; the next square-integral split should allow sample-point-dependent increment moduli.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the path-dependent-modulus variation-bound endpoint `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_sq_terminal_eq_zero_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound_eventual_modulus`. It moves the increment modulus inside the almost-sure event, chooses the sample-point sequence, reuses `BoundedVariationOn.sq_increment_sum_tendsto_zero_of_uniform_bound`, and delegates to the closed refining-partition endpoint.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the finite-maximum wrapper `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_sq_terminal_eq_zero_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound_sup_modulus`. It uses the `NNReal` finite supremum of partition increment norms as the sample-point modulus and delegates to the path-dependent-modulus endpoint.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `UniformContinuousOn.finite_partition_sup_nnnorm_sub_tendsto_zero`, `ContinuousOn.uniformContinuousOn_Icc`, and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_sq_terminal_eq_zero_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound_uniformContinuousOn`. These close the explicit entourage-mesh to pathwise maximum-increment bridge and the variation-bounded square-integral endpoint under pathwise uniform continuity.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integral_sq_terminal_eq_zero_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound_continuousOn` and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound_continuousOn`. These convert pathwise continuity on compact order intervals into the uniform-continuity hypothesis for the explicit-mesh square-integral endpoint, then turn the zero square integral into terminal a.e. zero.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_on_event_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound_continuousOn` and `MeasureTheory.ae_eq_zero_of_eventually_event_zero_exhaustion`. These transfer the bounded continuous explicit-mesh terminal zero conclusion from a localized martingale to an original process on one event, then remove countably many localization events when they cover almost every sample point.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_localized_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound_continuousOn` and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_stoppedProcess_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound_continuousOn`. These package the event-localized zero theorem over countably many covering events and specialize it to stopped/indicator localizations on events `{ω | (t : WithTop κ) < τ n ω}`.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `ProbabilityTheory.IsLocalizingSequence.eventually_exists_gt` and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_localizingSequence_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_of_variation_bound_continuousOn`. These derive the fixed-time cover from `hτ.tendsto_top`, derive stopped/indicator true martingales from `MeasureTheory.Martingale.stoppedProcess_indicator`, and delegate to the stopped-process zero theorem while keeping deterministic bounds, variation bounds, continuity, partitions, and mesh explicit.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the stopped/indicator pathwise and a.e. bound-transfer layer: `MeasureTheory.stoppedProcess_indicator_bound_on_Icc`, `BoundedVariationOn.eVariationOn_stoppedProcess_indicator_le_Icc`, `BoundedVariationOn.stoppedProcess_indicator_variation_bound_on_Icc`, and `MeasureTheory.ae_stoppedProcess_indicator_bound_variation_on_Icc`. These transfer deterministic horizon bounds and deterministic variation bounds from an original path to its stopped/indicator path, then package the transfer under almost-sure hypotheses.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_of_localizingSequence_of_bound_variation_bound_continuousOn`. For each localizing time, it applies `MeasureTheory.ae_stoppedProcess_indicator_bound_variation_on_Icc` to convert