 t` to make the jump `N t - N_{t-}` past-measurable.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the generated-past zero-integral package `MeasureTheory.Filtration.ae_eq_zero_of_past_setIntegral_eq_zero` and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.ae_eq_leftLim_of_left_approach_past_setIntegral_zero`. The first extends zero set integrals from the linearly ordered strict-past filtration generator to the generated past sigma-algebra by pi-system induction and concludes a.e. zero; the second applies it to the predictable finite-variation jump under explicit integrability and earlier-set zero-integral hypotheses.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the analytic jump set-integral package `MeasureTheory.Martingale.setIntegral_increment_eq_zero_of_measurableSet` and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.setIntegral_jump_leftLim_eq_zero_of_left_approach_of_dominated`. The first proves future martingale increments have zero set integral over earlier-filtration events; the second passes this identity to the deterministic left jump by dominated convergence on a restricted measure, keeping the left-approach and domination hypotheses explicit.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides the bounded-horizon jump-removal package `Filter.Tendsto.eventually_const_le_of_nhdsWithin_Iio`, `MeasureTheory.norm_sub_le_two_mul_of_Icc_bound`, and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.ae_eq_leftLim_of_left_approach_past_setIntegral_zero_of_bound`. These instantiate the generated-past/dominated-jump machinery under an explicit left-approaching sequence, explicit jump integrability, and an a.e. deterministic horizon bound.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.Martingale.integrable_jump_leftLim_of_left_approach_of_bound` and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.ae_eq_leftLim_of_left_approach_past_setIntegral_zero_of_bound_no_integrability`. These remove the separate jump-integrability hypothesis from bounded-horizon jump removal by deriving integrability from the same explicit deterministic left-approaching sequence and a.e. deterministic horizon bound.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.Martingale.ae_eq_leftLim_stoppedProcess_indicator_of_left_approach_of_bound` and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.ae_eq_leftLim_localizingSequence_stoppedProcess_indicator_of_left_approach_of_bound`. These specialize bounded-horizon jump removal to stopped/indicator processes and localizing families by transferring martingales, predictability, local bounded variation, and deterministic horizon bounds through existing stopped-process lemmas, while still keeping the deterministic left-approaching sequence and a.e. horizon bounds explicit.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.stoppedProcess_indicator_eventuallyEq_left_of_lt`, `MeasureTheory.leftLim_stoppedProcess_indicator_eq_of_lt`, `MeasureTheory.Martingale.ae_eq_leftLim_on_event_of_left_approach_of_bound`, and `MeasureTheory.Martingale.ae_eq_leftLim_localizingSequence_of_left_approach_of_bound`. These transfer stopped/indicator jump removal back to the original process on `{ω | (t : WithTop κ) < τ n ω}` and then use the localizing-sequence cover to obtain deterministic jump removal for the original martingale under explicit left-approach and horizon-bound hypotheses.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.Martingale.eq_zero_and_leftLim_eq_zero_of_localizingSequence_of_bound_variation_bound_original_continuousOn`. It composes the localizing-sequence terminal-zero wrapper with the localizing-sequence jump-removal theorem to obtain both `N t = 0` and `Function.leftLim (N · ω) t = 0` almost surely under explicit deterministic left-approach, original horizon-bound, variation-bound, pathwise-continuity, partition, and mesh hypotheses.\n- `BrownianMotion/StochasticIntegral/DoobMeyer.lean` now provides `MeasureTheory.Martingale.ae_e