{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014MapdWfVxdeuhjfJaiVtpK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Strategy Critic Report\n2\t\n3\t## Slug\n4\tqv-route\n5\t\n6\t## Iteration\n7\t062\n8\t\n9\t## Routes audited\n10\t\n11\tSTRATEGY.md declares a single route (\"Single route through the Brownian dependency chain\").\n12\tI audit that route, then handle the focus request, the format block, the deferral findings,\n13\tand the alternatives.\n14\t\n15\t### Route: Single Brownian dependency chain (QV = predictable part of Doob–Meyer of `X²`)\n16\t\n17\t- **Goal-alignment**: PARTIAL — the route does reach `quadraticVariation_brownian`, but the\n18\t  *active milestone it leads with* (predictable finite-variation uniqueness) is NOT the binding\n19\t  constraint. `quadraticVariation_brownian` (QuadraticVariationBrownian.lean:376) transitively\n20\t  needs all three sorries closed: `isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm` (QuadraticVariation.lean:84),\n21\t  `doob_meyer` (DoobMeyer.lean:3747), and the FV-uniqueness `_reduction` (DoobMeyer.lean:3525).\n22\t  Finishing only the FV-uniqueness phase the strategy makes \"active\" produces **zero end-to-end\n23\t  unblock** — the theorem stays sorry-bound on the other two. Leading with the most-invested link\n24\t  rather than the binding one is a sequencing miss.\n25\t- **Mathematical soundness**: PASS — the math is correct. The kernel is correctly identified:\n26\t  `eq_zero_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_core` (DoobMeyer.lean:3462) isolates the trivial\n27\t  tail (`∫ Nₜ² = 0 ⟹ Nₜ =ᵐ 0` via `ae_eq_zero_of_integral_sq_eq_zero`), and increment\n28\t  orthogonality is already available (`integral_increment_mul_increment_eq_zero`). The classical\n29\t  L² mesh estimate `E[Nₜ²] = Σ E[(N_{t_{i+1}}−N_{t_i})²] ≤ E[maxᵢ|ΔN|·V_t] → 0` is the right\n30\t  argument and is partially scaffolded.\n31\t- **Sunk-cost reasoning detected**: yes — see Sunk-cost flags. The Routes paragraph justifies the\n32\t  phase or