4\t  submartingale\", then \"doob_meyer\") implicitly multiplies the iter count.\n55\t- **Verdict**: CHALLENGE\n56\t\n57\t## Format compliance\n58\t\n59\t- **Size**: ≈60 lines / well under budget — within budget (~250 lines / ~12 KB).\n60\t- **Headings**: PASS — `## Goal`, `## Phases & estimations`, `## Routes`, `## Open strategic\n61\t  questions`, `## Mathlib gaps & new material`, in canonical order. (`## References index` and\n62\t  `## Blueprint summary` in the directive are the *directive's* sections, not part of STRATEGY.md.)\n63\t- **Per-iter narrative detected**: no literal `iter-NNN` references.\n64\t- **Accumulation detected**: yes — the `## Routes` section is a single run-on sentence\n65\t  enumerating ~20 *closed* helper lemmas (\"Predictable-jump bookkeeping through the generated past\n66\t  sigma-algebra, bounded-horizon domination, bounded jump integrability, … are closed.\"). A list\n67\t  of completed sub-lemmas is per-iter progress accumulation; it belongs in iter sidecars, not in\n68\t  the route description. The route should state the *remaining* path, not a changelog of closed\n69\t  helpers.\n70\t- **Table discipline**: PASS structurally (all six columns, LOC carries both figures), but six of\n71\t  nine rows read `~0/it` — see effort honesty.\n72\t- **Format verdict**: DRIFTED — the accumulation in `## Routes` is the one material deviation;\n73\t  compress it to the remaining path.\n74\t\n75\t## Infrastructure-deferral findings\n76\t\n77\t### Deferred: `ProbabilityTheory.IsLocalSubmartingale.doob_meyer` (local Doob–Meyer existence)\n78\t\n79\t- **Required by goal**: yes — the directive names it as obligation (3); `quadraticVariation` is\n80\t  *defined* as `(doob_meyer_normalized …).choose_spec.choose` (DoobMeyer.lean:3810,\n81\t  QuadraticVariation.lean:109), so `quadraticVariation_brownian` cannot be sorry-free without it.\n82\t- **Current plan for building it**: row 3 marks it \"blocked on core inputs\" at `≈420 · ~0/it`,\n83\t  with prerequisites (Class D, càdlàg modification, Komlós, localization, normalization)\n84\t  themselves rows at `~0/it`. No row shows realized progress on this sub-tree.\n85\t- **Timeline**: vague — `6–12` iters at `~0/it` realized is not a credible timeline; the\n86\t  prerequisite phases have no concrete start.\n87\t- **Verdict**: CHALLENGE — this is the project's true binding constraint and it is stagnant while\n88\t  effort flows to the non-binding FV-uniqueness link. Either start a concrete prover lane on the\n89\t  `doob_meyer` sub-tree (decomposed into the Komlós / càdlàg-modification / Class-D sub-phases this\n90\t  iter) or explicitly re-sequence so the active destination is gated on it.\n91\t\n92\t### Deferred: the FV-uniqueness wrapper tower → single `_reduction` sorry\n93\t\n94\t- **Required by goal**: partially — *a* proof of FV-uniqueness is required; the **tower** is not.\n95\t- **Current plan**: DoobMeyer.lean 3489–3684 is a chain — `_reduction` (the lone sorry, 3525) →\n96\t  `_bounded_continuous` (3533, just calls `_reduction`) → `_value_zero` (3553, builds left-limit +\n97\t  past-increment `have`s, discards them via `_…_used`, calls `_bounded_continuous`) →\n98\t  `_past_condExp_zero` (3596, `condExp` of `_value_zero`) → `_noninitial_analytic` (3616) →\n99\t  `_noninitial` (3639) → `_finiteVariation` (3668). The middle lemmas add **no** mathematical\n100\t  content: `_value_zero`/`_noninitial_analytic`/`_past_condExp_zero` set up hypotheses, immediately\n101\t  shelve them, and forward to the next layer, and `_past_condExp_zero ↔ _value_zero` is circular\n102\t  (condExp-zero derived from value-zero, value-zero \"derived\" from condExp-zero).\n103\t- **Timeline**: the `≈70 · ~20/it` figure measures wrapper/helper churn, not the unproven core.\n104\t- **Verdict**: CHALLENGE — the ~20 closed helpers and the wrapper tower keep renaming the hard\n105\t  analytic core (the one `_reduction` sorry) without shrinking it. Collapse the dead wrappers and\n106\t  point effort at the single mesh/orthogonality estimate that is the only real content.\n107\t\n108\t## Alternative routes (suggested)\n109\t\n110\t### Alternative: prove a *continuous*-hypothesis FV-uniqueness, drop the jump machinery\n111\t\n112\t- **What it looks like**: state the bridge with `∀ ω, ContinuousOn (N · ω) (Icc ⊥ t)` (which the\n113\t  `core` lemma at 3462 already assumes) instead of càdlàg-`hN_cadlag` + `IsStronglyPredictable` +\n114\t  jump removal. For a continuous bounded FV martingale started at 0 the proof is exactly the mesh\n115\t  estimate on `[0,t]` with deterministic partitions — no predictable-jump removal, no\n116\t  generated-past sigma-algebra, no left-isolated/bottom-immediate/dense-left/strict-predecessor\n117\t  case split. In the Brownian application `A₀ − A` *is* continuous (`B²` is continuous, so its\n118\t  Doob–Meyer predictable part is continuous, and `A = t` is continuous), so the jump branches are\n119\t  **vacuous** there.\n120\t- **Why it might be cheaper or sounder**: the entire order-theoretic case analysis on a general\n121\t  `PolishSpace`-ordered `κ` (the source of the ~20 helpers) exists only to handle jumps and\n122\t  isolated/discrete time points that `ℝ≥0` and the continuous Brownian application never produce.\n123\t  A `ℝ≥0`/dense-order, continuous-paths statement is the textbook Karatzas–Shreve argument and is a\n124\t  fraction of the LOC.\n125\t- **What the current strategy may have rejected**: it appears to be chasing the fully general\n126\t  càdlàg-predictable statement for eventual reuse — open questions #4/#5 show the planner is aware\n127\t  the general-`κ` branch is what spawns the jump/predecessor complexity but has not committed to\n128\t  splitting it off.\n129\t- **Severity of the omission**: major\n130\t\n131\t### Alternative: decouple the Brownian milestone from full Doob–Meyer existence\n132\t\n133\t- **What it looks like**: `quadraticVariation` is currently *defined* through the general\n134\t  `doob_meyer` existence theorem, so the fixed-time Brownian result inherits the entire Doob–Meyer\n135\t  monster (Komlós + càdlàg modification + Class D + optional sampling) as a hard prerequisite. For\n136\t  Brownian motion the answer is explicit: `B_t² − t` is already a martingale\n137\t  (`martingale_brownian_sq_sub_time`) and `t` is a continuous predictable increasing FV process\n138\t  from 0 — i.e. `t` is a normalized predictable part *by inspection*. Define the Brownian QV\n139\t  directly (as `t`, or as the ucp/L² limit of `Σ(B_{t_{i+1}}−B_{t_i})²`, the textbook definition)\n140\t  and prove `quadraticVariation_brownian` via Itô-isometry/mesh, gated only on FV-*uniqueness*\n141\t  (to identify the abstract predictable part with `t`) rather than on Doob–Meyer *existence*.\n142\t- **Why it might be cheaper or sounder**: it removes the ≈420-LOC `~0/it` `doob_meyer` existence\n143\t  theorem (and its Komlós/càdlàg/Class-D sub-tree) from the critical path of the *currently active\n144\t  destination*. The general Doob–Meyer definition is defensible for the eventual semimartingale/Itô\n145\t  goal, but binding the Brownian fixed-time milestone to the project's single largest stagnant\n146\t  phase is what makes the milestone unreachable.\n147\t- **What the current strategy may have rejected**: the strategy commits to \"Single route\" with\n148\t  QV ≡ Doob–Meyer predictable part and lists no alternative QV definition; this trade-off is not\n149\t  surfaced anywhere in STRATEGY.md.\n150\t- **Severity of the omission**: major\n151\t\n152\t## Sunk-cost flags\n153\t\n154\t- `\"… are closed. The current milestone constructs concrete leastGT norm-level pre-stop and finite\n155\t  stop-value bounds; after that, construct closed-pre-stop variation-level inputs …\"` — Why this is\n156\t  sunk-cost: the route is justified and sequenced by the volume of already-closed helper lemmas,\n157\t  making the most-invested link the lead \"active\" phase even though closing it unblocks nothing\n158\t  end-to-end (two other sorries gate the goal). Recommendation: sequence by binding constraint\n159\t  (`doob_meyer` existence and `isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm`), not by accumulated helper count, and\n160\t  move the closed-helper enumeration out of `## Routes`.\n161\t\n162\t## Must-fix-this-iter\n163\t\n164\t- Route (single chain): CHALLENGE — re-sequence so effort targets the binding constraints.\n165\t  Completing the FV-uniqueness phase alone leaves `quadraticVariation_brownian` sorry-bound;\n166\t  `isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm` and `doob_meyer` must also be addressed. Either parallelize the\n167\t  three independent sorries or justify the ordering with an explicit rebuttal in plan.md.\n168\t- Infrastructure-deferral CHALLENGE — `doob_meyer` existence is required by the goal, sits at\n169\t  `~0/it`, and its prerequisites (Komlós, càdlàg modification, Class D) are also `~0/it`. Start a\n170\t  concrete prover lane decomposed into those sub-phases this iter, or re-sequence the active\n171\t  destination to depend on it explicitly with an iter estimate.\n172\t- Infrastructure-deferral CHALLENGE — collapse the FV-uniqueness pass-through tower\n173\t  (`_value_zero`/`_noninitial_analytic`/`_past_condExp_zero` add no content and are circular) and\n174\t  point effort at the single `_reduction` mesh/orthogonality estimate.\n175\t- Alternative (continuous-hypothesis FV-uniqueness): major omission — the general-`κ` jump-removal\n176\t  machinery is vacuous in the continuous Brownian application; evaluate a continuous-paths /\n177\t  dense-order statement that drops the order-theoretic case split.\n178\t- Alternative (decouple Brownian milestone from Doob–Meyer existence): major omission — the active\n179\t  destination inherits the project's largest stagnant phase purely through the QV *definition*;\n180\t  evaluate a direct Brownian QV definition gated on uniqueness, not existence.\n181\t- Format: DRIFTED — compress the `## Routes` closed-helper enumeration to the remaining path; move\n182\t  the changelog of closed lemmas to an iter sidecar.\n183\t\n184\t## Overall verdict\n185\t\n186\tThe single route is mathematically sound and reaches the stated theorem, and the analytic kernel\n187\t(increment orthogonality + the `∫ Nₜ²=0` core) is correctly identified — so this is not a REJECT.\n188\tBut the strategy commits two infrastructure-deferral patterns the planner must address. First, the\n189\tstrategy defers `doob_meyer` (the local Doob–Meyer existence theorem), which is required for the\n190\tstated goal — `quadraticVariation` is defined through it — yet it sits at `~0/it` \"blocked\" behind\n191\tprerequisites that are themselves `~0/it`, while effort flows to the non-binding FV-uniqueness link\n192\tthat, even when finished, unblocks nothing end-to-end. Second, the FV-uniqueness tower renames the\n193\thard analytic core through a stack of pass-through/circular wrappers and ~20 order-theoretic helper\n194\tlemmas whose generality (general `PolishSpace`-ordered `κ`, predictable jumps) is vacuous in the\n195\tcontinuous Brownian application. Two major alternatives go unmentioned: a continuous-hypothesis\n196\tFV-uniqueness that deletes the jump/predecessor case split, and decoupling the Brownian milestone\n197\tfrom full Doob–Meyer existence by defining the QV directly for this case. Re-sequence by binding\n198\tconstraint, parallelize the three independent sorries, and compress the accumulated `## Routes`\n199\tchangelog.\n200\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c68c3a1-ce96-4aaa-9a82-bf5af151dc85","uuid":"8add8a12-cfde-4acb-aa35-31fe6abb6e02","timestamp":"2026-06-09T12:30:14.106Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/firefly/code/nus/math/brownian-motion/.archon/task_results/strategy-critic-qv-route.md","content":"# Strategy Critic Report\n\n## Slug\nqv-route\n\n## Iteration\n062\n\n## Routes audited\n\nSTRATEGY.md declares a single route (\"Single route through the Brownian dependency chain\").\nI audit that route, then handle the focus request, the format block, the deferral findings,\nand the alternatives.\n\n### Route: Single Brownian dependency chain (QV = predictable part of Doob–Meyer of `X²`)\n\n- **Goal-alignment**: PARTIAL — the route does reach `quadraticVariation_brownian`, but the\n  *active milestone it leads with* (predictable finite-variation uniqueness) is NOT the binding\n  constraint. `quadraticVariation_brownian` (QuadraticVariationBrownian.lean:376) transitively\n  needs all three sorries closed: `isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm` (QuadraticVariation.lean:84),\n  `doob_meyer` (DoobMeyer.lean:3747), and the FV-uniqueness `_reduction` (DoobMeyer.lean:3525).\n  Finishing only the FV-uniqueness phase the strategy makes \"active\" produces **zero end-to-end\n  unblock** — the theorem stays sorry-bound on the other two. Leading with the most-invested link\n  rather than the binding one is a sequencing miss.\n- **Mathematical soundness**: PASS — the math is correct. The kernel is correctly identified:\n  `eq_zero_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_core` (DoobMeyer.lean:3462) isolates the trivial\n  tail (`∫ Nₜ² = 0 ⟹ Nₜ =ᵐ 0` via `ae_eq_zero_of_integral_sq_eq_zero`), and increment\n  orthogonality is already available (`integral_increment_mul_increment_eq_zero`). The classical\n  L² mesh estimate `E[Nₜ²] = Σ E[(N_{t_{i+1}}−N_{t_i})²] ≤ E[maxᵢ|ΔN|·V_t] → 0` is the right\n  argument and is partially scaffolded.\n- **Sunk-cost reasoning detected**: yes — see Sunk-cost flags. The Routes paragraph justifies the\n  phase ordering by enumerating ~20 *already-closed* helper lemmas, and makes the phase with that\n  accumulated momentum the lead \"active\" phase even though it is the last (non-binding) link.\n- **Infrastructure-deferral detected**: yes — two distinct patterns (see findings): (i) the\n  `doob_meyer` existence theorem (required by the goal) sits at `~0/it` \"blocked on core inputs\"\n  whose own inputs (Komlós, càdlàg modification, Class D) are also `~0/it`; (ii) the FV-uniqueness\n  tower is a stack of pass-through wrappers that funnel into a single `sorry` while renaming the\n  hard analytic core (see focus response).\n- **Phantom prerequisites**: none detected. Mathlib has no general \"continuous FV martingale is\n  constant\" / Doob–Meyer / continuous-martingale QV result, so the project-built kernel is\n  appropriate, not a missing-infra bet. The project-internal lemmas in the chain\n  (`integral_increment_mul_increment_eq_zero`, `ae_eq_zero_of_integral_sq_eq_zero`,\n  `stronglyMeasurable_past`) compile, hence exist.\n- **Effort honesty**: under-counted on the back half. Rows 3–9 (`doob_meyer`, UI/optional\n  sampling, càdlàg modification, Komlós, sq-integrable convergence, Borel foundations, polish)\n  all carry `~0/it` realized velocity. A row claiming `Iters left: 6–12` with `~0/it` realized is\n  internally inconsistent: at the observed velocity it never completes. The honest reading is that\n  only the top two rows are moving and the binding constraint (`doob_meyer`, ≈420 LOC) has shown\n  no realized progress.\n- **Parallelism under-exploited**: yes — the three open sorries are largely independent.\n  `isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm` (a local-square-integrability/Jensen argument, QV.lean:84) shares\n  no dependency with the FV-uniqueness bridge, and `doob_meyer` existence is independent of\n  FV-uniqueness. Serializing them (\"Predictable FV uniqueness\" first, then \"square-norm\n  submartingale\", then \"doob_meyer\") implicitly multiplies the iter count.\n- **Verdict**: CHALLENGE\n\n## Format compliance\n\n- **Size**: ≈60 lines / well under budget — within budget (~250 lines / ~12 KB).\n- **Headings**: PASS — `## Goal`, `## Phases & estimations`, `## Routes`, `## Open strategic\n  questions`, `## Mathlib gaps & new material`, in canonical order. (`## References index` and\n  `## Blueprint summary` in the directive are the *directive's* sections, not part of STRATEGY.md.)\