{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HyeSjfpwyjqn5TA5PQ6zdp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Mathlib Analogist Report\n2\t\n3\t## Mode\n4\tapi-alignment\n5\t\n6\t## Slug\n7\tfv-uniqueness\n8\t\n9\t## Iteration\n10\t062\n11\t\n12\t## Question\n13\t\n14\t(1) Does Mathlib already have \"a continuous (local) martingale of finite variation is a.e.\n15\tconstant\", or directly composable pieces (a continuous FV process has zero quadratic variation; a\n16\tcontinuous local martingale with zero QV is constant)? If so the project's chain is a parallel API.\n17\t(2) Is the chosen generality (arbitrary linearly-ordered `κ` with `WithTop`/`leastGT`/explicit\n18\tmesh/partition + dense/bottom-immediate/left-isolated branch disjunctions) idiomatic for Mathlib's\n19\tmartingale / FV / QV API, or is it re-deriving real-time analysis Mathlib already has? Quantify the\n20\tcost.\n21\t\n22\t## Verdicts (summary)\n23\t\n24\t| Decision | Verdict | Severity |\n25\t|---|---|---|\n26\t| Core FV-uniqueness / QV pieces exist in Mathlib? | NEEDS_MATHLIB_GAP_FILL | informational |\n27\t| Foundational process layer over general κ (filtration/stopping/predictable/variation) | DIVERGE_INTENTIONALLY (aligned) | informational |\n28\t| Analytic core over general κ vs. specialize to ℝ≥0 | ALIGN_WITH_MATHLIB (specialize) | critical |\n29\t\n30\t## Must-fix-this-iter\n31\t\n32\t- **Analytic core generality**: the load-bearing `sorry` at\n33\t  `DoobMeyer.lean:3525` (`eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation_bounded_continuous_reduction`) and\n34\t  its premise `eq_zero_of_bounded_continuous_finiteVariation_core` (line 3462) should be closed\n35\t  **specialized to `κ = ℝ≥0`** (or `[0,t] ⊆ ℝ`), not over general `κ`. The sole consumer is Brownian\n36\t  over `ℝ≥0` (`QuadraticVariationBrownian.lean:24`), which is `DenselyOrdered`\n37\t  (`Mathlib/Data/NNReal/Defs.lean:84,397`) — so the bottom-immediate and left-isolated branches are\n38\t  vacuous for the real targ