{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KrSbDUasdXDUUsFFBf3a9z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I now understand the deep issue: the general-`κ` `_reduction` is essentially **unprovable as stated** — closing it requires constructing a deterministic refining partition with vanishing mesh on `[⊥,t]`, which is impossible in an arbitrary linear order. That is exactly why every endpoint in the chain takes the partition as an *explicit hypothesis* and defers it — and `_reduction` is where the buck stops. This confirms both critics: the route must specialize to densely-ordered time, and the helper treadmill was deferring the one construction that forces specialization.\n\nLet me record decisions and rewrite the strategy. First, STRATEGY.md:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5557,"cache_read_input_tokens":140873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5557},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c68c3a1-ce96-4aaa-9a82-bf5af151dc85","uuid":"d12fa15d-cfca-4342-a4f2-277f4e0839e6","request_id":"req_011CbshBFBQKhUUbG8PWC8E2"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01KrSbDUasdXDUUsFFBf3a9z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0187LmzV6sDq4m5Z9e1qdZKF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/firefly/code/nus/math/brownian-motion/.archon/STRATEGY.md","content":"# Strategy\n\n## Goal\n\nEliminate the remaining `sorry` terms while preserving the intended mathematical surface. The fixed-time Brownian quadratic-variation theorem `ProbabilityTheory.quadraticVariation_brownian` has landed as a Lean declaration but is still `sorry`-bound transitively through THREE independent generic obligations, ALL of which must close for the goal to be sorry-free: (1) squared-norm local submartingales (`IsLocalMartingale.isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm`, QV.lean), (2) predictable finite-variation uniqueness (`Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable_finiteVariation_bounded_continuous_reduction`, DoobMeyer.lean), and (3) the weak local Doob–Meyer existence theorem (`IsLocalSubmartingale.doob_meyer`, DoobMeyer.lean). Beyond this milestone the destination is the stochastic integral and Itô's lemma.\n\n## Phases & estimations\n\n| Phase | Status | Iters left | LOC (remaining · realized/it) | Key Mathlib needs | Risks |\n| --- | --- | ---: | --- | --- | --- |\n| FV-uniqueness reduction (`_reduction`) | PIVOTED — specialize to dense time + assemble | 2–4 | ≈90 · ~0/it net | deterministic refining partition w/ vanishing mesh on `[⊥,t]`; Heine–Cantor | General-`κ` statement is unprovable: no partition exists in an arbitrary order — must specialize |\n| Square-norm local submartingale | needs signature repair first | 2–4 | ≈60 · ~0/it | bounded-stopping/local square-integrability under finite measure | Present global signature is too weak; decide repaired statement before proving |\n| Local Doob–Meyer existence (`doob_meyer`) | binding & stagnant | 6–12 | ≈420 · ~0/it | Class D, càdlàg modification, Komlós, localization | Largest phase; `quadraticVariation` is *defined* through it — see route question on decoupling |\n| Uniform integrability, optional sampling, local stability | queued, ordered | 4–8 | ≈200 · ~0/it | UI closure; conditional-expectation order; discrete approximation | General-index transfer has heavy typeclass constraints |\n| Càdlàg modification theorem | queued | 3–6 | ≈180 · ~0/it | upcrossing/simple-process bounds; countable exceptional set | Mathematically large source theorem |\n| Komlós convergence chain | ready, ordered | 4–8 | ≈260 · ~0/it | Hilbert convex tails; `Lp` convergence; measurability | Final `ENNReal` statement has a measurability TODO |\n| Square-integrable martingale convergence | queued | 2–4 | ≈120 · ~0/it | martingale convergence; `eLpNorm` identities | Time-index generality may exceed Mathlib |\n| Borel and compact-system foundations | deferred | 2–4 | ≈100 · ~0/it | sum/sigma Borel spaces; compact-system closure | Off the current Brownian route |\n| Final polish and audit | pending proofs | 1–2 | ≈40 · ~0/it | lints, axiom audit, blueprint sync | Build passes but permits known sorries |\n\n## Routes\n\nSingle route through the Brownian dependency chain, but the three gating sorries above are **independent** and should be worked in parallel lanes, not serialized. The Brownian martingale `B_t² − t`, the deterministic-time predictable part, the discrete predictable-jump uniqueness, the conditional-expectation/past-measurability reductions, the jump-removal pipeline, and the continuous-paths localizing endpoints (which take the partition + mesh as explicit hypotheses) are all closed. The remaining FV-uniqueness work is NOT more helpers: it is to *assemble* those closed endpoints into `_reduction`, specialized to densely-ordered time so the one genuinely missing construction — a deterministic refining partition with vanishing mesh on `[⊥,t]` — becomes constructible (dyadics on ℝ≥0 / dense order + Heine–Cantor uniform continuity). Sequencing is by binding constraint (`doob_meyer` existence and `isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm` gate the goal as hard as FV-uniqueness does), not by accumulated helper count.\n\n## Open strategic questions\n\n- **Decouple the Brownian milestone from full Doob–Meyer existence?** `quadraticVariation` is currently *defined* through `doob_meyer_normalized`, so the Brownian fixed-time result inherits the ≈420-LOC stagnant `doob_meyer` existence theorem (+ Komlós/càdlàg-modification/Class-D) as a hard prerequisite. For Brownian motion the predictable part is explicit (`t`), so a direct definition of `brownianQuadraticVariation` gated only on FV-*uniqueness* (not existence) would remove the largest stagnant phase from the active critical path. Recommended next pivot; requires a definition-level refactor (out of scope for the reassessment iter). [from strategy-critic]\n- **Specialization target for FV-uniqueness: `[DenselyOrdered κ]` + existing topological instances, or all the way to `κ = ℝ≥0`?** The dense-order route matches the existing endpoint instances with one added instance; the ℝ≥0 route is concrete (dyadics) but re-states the chain. Prover may choose; dense-order preferred.\n- Should `isLocalSubmartingale_sq_norm` be replaced by a usual-condition version (its current global signature is too weak for the proof route), or should both variants coexist?\n- Should the FV-uniqueness chain keep a continuity hypothesis (the Brownian application is continuous, jump branches vacuous) or retain càdlàg+predictable with derived continuity? [from strategy-critic alt-a]\n- `leastGT` is a project-local reimplementation overlapping Mathlib's `hittingAfter`/`hittingBtwn` — minor candidate parallel API; revisit only if `leastGT` work resumes. [from mathlib-analogist]\n- Is the raw Brownian natural filtration intended to be completed/right-continuized, or kept as an explicit usual-condition context?\n- Does Mathlib now contain a submartingale stopped-value uniform-integrability theorem subsuming the local result?\n\n## Mathlib gaps & new material\n\n**Gaps to fill**\n\n- Deterministic refining partition with vanishing mesh on a compact dense-ordered interval (the construction `_reduction` cannot make over general `κ`).\n- Local square-integrable bounded-stopping localization for càdlàg local martingales under finite measure.\n- Continuous-time Doob–Meyer / \"continuous FV martingale is constant\" — confirmed ABSENT from Mathlib (only ℕ-indexed `predictablePart`/`martingalePart` and `Martingale.eq_zero_of_predictable'` exist); the project must build the kernel, there is no shorter idiom. [mathlib-analogist]\n- Borel-space instances for binary and countable dependent sums; compact-system closure.\n- Optional sampling, càdlàg modification, and Komlós convergence inputs for local Doob–Meyer.\n\n**New project material**\n\n- FV-uniqueness reduction `_reduction` assembled from the closed jump-removal + continuous-localizing endpoints, specialized to dense time.\n- Quadratic variation as the normalized predictable part of the local Doob–Meyer decomposition (and the candidate direct Brownian definition).\n- Normalized choice layer + usual-condition shift helpers for the Doob–Meyer predictable part.\n- Stopping/localization stability for càdlàg, predictable, finite-variation processes.\n- Martingale increment orthogonality and bounded-continuous finite-partition square-integral helpers.\n- Uniform integrability and square-integrable convergence helpers for stopped martingales.\n- Brownian quadratic variation via the canonical Brownian martingale, up to a.e./indistinguishability equality.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5557,"cache_read_input_tokens":140873,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5557},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessio